// The warning (yellow) aspect: a green signal whose booked road ends at or
// before the next signal. It is drawn as that signal's own green with the lamp
// repainted, so what is needed is a recolour map and not a picture of every
// signal there is: the green ramp (palette 0xCE to 0xD1) goes to the amber one
// (0xBB to 0xBE) and everything else is left alone.
//
// That way it costs one sprite instead of one per kind of signal, it holds for
// every kind and both variants, and it works on whatever green the base set or
// a NewGRF signal set happens to draw -- a set with no picture of its own for
// the aspect gets one that matches the rest of its signals rather than ours.
//
// The amber tops out at 0xBE and starts deep at 0xBB, so a semaphore's
// repainted lamp cannot be taken for the always-yellow lamp below it, which
// runs 0x32 to 0x34 from (252,208,0) upwards.
//
// Second in this block on purpose. A base set may supply recolour sprites of
// its own -- OpenGFX supplies exactly one, the all-black map above -- and a
// block that short cannot reach this one.
